<% content_for :title, "Loan Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Loan calculator page (spec issue #185, DESIGN.md BLEND) — a fixed-rate amortizing loan
  that generalizes Amortization with a solve-for MODE PICKER. The picker selects which of
  three unknowns to solve for (the monthly payment, the affordable loan amount, or the
  term); only that mode's two GIVEN figures show, and the page solves the third. The form
  posts over Turbo and re-renders the #result region in place; it works WITHOUT JS — the
  server validates exactly the selected mode's required fields and re-renders the result
  fragment. Stimulus is pure polish: it reveals only the active mode's given fields
  (disabling the rest so the solved-for field is never posted) and lifts the active row.

  Mode-picker choice (DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker"): THREE modes, but the labels are
  multi-word / long ("Monthly payment", "Loan amount"). The §4 rule reserves the segmented
  control for N ≤ 3 with SHORT labels (≈≤12 chars); a multi-word label routes to the
  SELECTABLE OPTION LIST (.mode-option) — which also gives each mode a helper line naming
  the two figures it is GIVEN (spec Notes). It stays a native radio <fieldset>/<legend>
  posting a single-select inputs[mode].

  Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing to
  one column on mobile. Spacing scale ("targets not minimums"):
    • stacked fields → space-y-5
    • major blocks within the card (mode → fields → submit) → mt-8 (Section tier)
    • column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier)
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Financial</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Loan Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    An amortized fixed-rate loan. Choose what to solve for — the
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">monthly payment</span>, the
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">loan amount</span> you can afford, or the
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">term</span> — enter the rest, and see the full
    repayment schedule. Every figure is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/loan", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "loan" } do |f| %>

      <%# Mode picker — selectable option list (.mode-option), per DESIGN.md §4: three
          multi-word "solve for" modes → one bordered, divided container of full-width rows,
          NOT a segmented control (reserved for N ≤ 3 short labels). The accessible control
          is a native radio <fieldset>/<legend> posting inputs[mode]; each radio is
          visually-hidden (peer sr-only) and paired to a styled <label for>. The active row
          is painted with no JS via peer:checked, and the .mode-option::before radio glyph is
          the non-colour active cue (DESIGN.md §6). Each row names what the mode SOLVES (bold
          label) and, on a helper line, the two figures it is GIVEN (spec Notes). %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Solve for…</legend>
        <div class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-[13px] border border-border-input divide-y divide-rule">
          <% loan_modes.each_with_index do |m, i| %>
            <div>
              <%= f.radio_button :mode, m[:value],
                    checked: i.zero?,
                    class: "peer sr-only",
                    data: { loan_target: "modeInput", action: "loan#select" } %>
              <%= f.label :mode, value: m[:value],
                    class: "mode-option",
                    data: { loan_target: "modeOption", mode: m[:value] } do %>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink"><%= m[:label] %></span>
                <span class="text-xs text-muted"><%= m[:helper] %></span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Given-figure fields. Each block declares the modes it serves (its mode is GIVEN
          that figure) via data-loan-modes; Stimulus shows only the active mode's blocks and
          disables the rest so the solved-for field is never submitted (the no-JS baseline
          shows all four — the server still reads only the mode's required fields). Stacked
          tier: space-y-5 down the column (DESIGN.md §3). Each input carries its $/%/unit
          affix on the Affix tier (gap-2 — DESIGN.md §3). %>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <%# Loan amount — given by payment + term modes. $ affix leading the field. %>
        <div data-loan-target="field" data-loan-modes="payment term">
          <%= f.label :loan_amount, "Loan amount", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_loan_amount" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :loan_amount, id: "inputs_loan_amount", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Monthly payment — given by amount + term modes. $ affix leading the field. %>
        <div data-loan-target="field" data-loan-modes="amount term">
          <%= f.label :monthly_payment, "Monthly payment", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_monthly_payment" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :monthly_payment, id: "inputs_monthly_payment", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Annual interest rate — given by every mode. % affix trailing the field. %>
        <div data-loan-target="field" data-loan-modes="payment amount term">
          <%= f.label :annual_rate, "Annual interest rate", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_annual_rate" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :annual_rate, id: "inputs_annual_rate", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">%</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Loan term — given by payment + amount modes. Whole months; a "months" unit
            trails the field. %>
        <div data-loan-target="field" data-loan-modes="payment amount">
          <%= f.label :term_months, "Loan term", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_term_months" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :term_months, id: "inputs_term_months", step: "1", inputmode: "numeric",
                  min: "1", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="w-14 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">months</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
